cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "fedcausal: federated causal discovery"
message: "If you use this software, please cite the FedGES paper below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Torrijos"
    given-names: "Pablo"
    affiliation: "Universidad de Castilla-La Mancha"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ptorrijos99/fedcausal"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
abstract: >-
  A Python implementation of federated causal discovery over two data regimes.
  FedGES learns Bayesian network structure from discrete data: each site runs
  greedy equivalence search on the data it holds, a coordinator combines the
  resulting graphs by structural consensus fusion, and only graphs and scores
  cross the network. FedRCD learns a causal order and linear coefficients from
  continuous data under a linear non-Gaussian model: each site reduces its
  rows to cumulant statistics, and only those statistics cross the network.
  Runs in-process for experiments and over Flower for deployment.
keywords:
  - causal discovery
  - structure learning
  - Bayesian networks
  - federated learning
  - greedy equivalence search
  - LiNGAM
  - cumulants

